You are a senior full-stack engineer delivering a minimal blog editor with markdown and autosave.

## Objective
Build a small blog app: markdown editor with autosave, store posts in Postgres via Drizzle, render at `/blog/[slug]`.

## Scope
- In-scope: project setup, DB schema/migration, CRUD for posts (create/read), editor with markdown preview + autosave, public post page.
- Out-of-scope: rich auth flows (basic session ok), image uploads, comments, SEO polish beyond basics.

## Tech Stack (fixed)
- Framework: Next.js 14 App Router (TypeScript)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Auth: Better Auth (lightweight) or simple in-memory mock if needed
- Database: PostgreSQL
- ORM: Drizzle ORM
- Markdown: `markdown-it` (+ `highlight.js` optional)
- Hosting: Vercel-compatible (optional)

## Constraints
- Minimal deps: Next, Tailwind, Drizzle, markdown-it, (optionally) highlight.js, zod.
- Follow RSC patterns; keep client components only where interactivity is required.
- Env via `.env` (`DATABASE_URL`).
- Make pragmatic defaults; no follow-up questions.

## Tasks (acceptance criteria)
1) Initialize Next.js 14 + Tailwind + Drizzle + Postgres connection.
2) Create `posts` table: `id (uuid)`, `title (text)`, `content (text)`, `slug (text unique)`, `created_at (timestamp)`, `updated_at (timestamp)`.
3) Build `/editor` page: title input, markdown textarea, live preview; autosave every 1.5s idle or on blur; create/update by slug.
4) Server actions for save (Drizzle), with validation (zod).
5) Public route `/blog/[slug]` renders markdown → HTML safely.
6) Minimal file tree, TS strict, ESLint/Prettier.
7) Seed one demo post.

## Data Model
- Post: { id, title, content, slug, created_at, updated_at }

## Routes
- `GET /blog/[slug]` → render a post
- `GET /editor?slug=optional` → create new or edit by slug
- `POST (server action) /actions/savePost` → upsert

## Output Requirements
- One-shot setup script (pnpm preferred) that: creates app, installs deps, configures Tailwind/Drizzle, creates migration, pushes schema, seeds.
- Full file-by-file code with exact paths.
- Verification steps: run, visit `/editor`, type, autosave, open `/blog/[slug]`.
- Sanity checklist confirming each task.

## Coding Style
- TS strict, lightweight client code only for editor.
- Accessible labels, `aria-*` where needed.
- No secret keys in code.

## Example Content
- Seed post: title “Hello Markdown”, slug `hello-markdown`, simple body.

## Deliverable Format (exact)
1. Plan
2. Setup (shell)
3. File tree
4. Code (each file with `// path: …`)
5. Verification
6. Sanity Checklist

Proceed with reasonable defaults if anything is unclear.
